			<_name type="a">Requirements.txt</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">12.31.1969::16:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1255\deff0\deflang1037{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 MS Sans Serif;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset177 MS Sans Serif;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\f0\fs17 textual requirements for the HomeAlarm\f1\rtlch\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">12.31.1969::16:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<m_path type="a">..\..</m_path>
			<m_type type="a">userFile</m_type>
			<AggregatesList type="e">
				<value>GUID 3ac52937-b8d2-49d9-960b-45d24a88e5fb</value>
			</AggregatesList>
		</IFile>
		<IFileFragment type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 3ac52937-b8d2-49d9-960b-45d24a88e5fb</_id>
			<_name type="a">Requirements</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">12.31.1969::16:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">12.31.1969::16:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<m_type type="a">textFragment</m_type>
			<m_text type="a">Can be armed / disarmed either via a remote control unit or via a %0D
simple keypad. When using a keypad to arm the alarm, a four-digit%0D
code must be entered followed by the on key. To disarm the alarm, %0D
a four-digit code must be entered followed by the off key.  It should%0D
be possible to change the code.%0D
When the alarm is armed and a presence is detected, the alarm%0D
will sound immediately. When arming the alarm, there is an exit %0D
delay to allow the homeowner to exit. When opening the door %0D
when the alarm is armed, there is an entry delay during which the %0D
homeowner can disarm the alarm, failing to do so will result in the %0D
alarm going off.%0D
The home alarm system should also be capable of switching lights %0D
on/off to simulate presence in the house.%0D
The alarm will have two LED's, one green and one red. %0D
The red led will indicate the alarm is active, %0D
the green will indicate that the alarm is powered up.%0D
</m_text>
			<m_startRow type="a">0</m_startRow>
			<m_startCol_Short type="a">0</m_startCol_Short>
			<m_endRow type="a">0</m_endRow>
			<m_endCol_Short type="a">0</m_endCol_Short>
